cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite the repository and the release used."
title: "Secure IoT Device Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rodríguez Fuertes"
    given-names: "Diego"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Research-grade ESP32 IoT device identity platform implementing manufacturing
  bootstrap, CSR-bound HMAC authentication, on-device P-256 key generation,
  X.509 enrollment, MQTT/mTLS authorization, certificate revocation, dashboard
  control, and realistic physical/simulated fleet testing.
keywords:
  - IoT
  - ESP32
  - cybersecurity
  - device identity
  - X.509
  - PKI
  - MQTT
  - mutual TLS
  - provisioning
  - bootstrapping
